---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { ANALYTICS, BRAND, CONTACT } from '../config';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy"
  description="What happens to the information you give Signalworks: it builds your draft, reaches our inbox, and goes nowhere else. Plain English, no legal maze."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <span class="eyebrow">Privacy</span>
      <h1>What happens to what you tell us.</h1>
      <p class="lede" style="margin-top: var(--space-4);">
        Short version: your intake answers exist to build your website. They
        go to our inbox, they don't get sold, and you can ask us to delete
        them anytime. The longer version below says the same thing with the
        details filled in.
      </p>

      <div class="stack" style="margin-top: var(--space-6);">
        <h2>What we collect</h2>
        <p>
          What you type into the intake or contact forms: business name,
          what you do, service area, phone, email, and the optional details
          you choose to add (photos, links, preferences). Nothing is
          collected behind your back — no hidden trackers scraping contacts.
        </p>

        <h2>Where it goes</h2>
        <p>
          Form submissions are delivered by a form-handling service to our
          email inbox, and that's where they live. The form service is a
          processor — it moves the message, it doesn't get to keep or use
          your information for itself. If you email or call directly, that
          conversation stays between us.
        </p>

        <h2>What we do with it</h2>
        <p>
          Build your draft, reply to you, and keep track of your project.
          That's the list. We don't sell your information, share it with
          advertisers, or add you to any mailing list you didn't ask for.
        </p>

        <h2>Analytics</h2>
        <p>
          {
            ANALYTICS.plausibleDomain
              ? 'We use privacy-friendly analytics (Plausible) that counts visits without cookies or personal profiles.'
              : 'If we add visitor analytics, it will be the privacy-friendly kind — page counts, not personal profiles — and this page will say so.'
          }
        </p>

        <h2>Deletion</h2>
        <p>
          Want your information gone? Email
          <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.email}`}>{CONTACT.email}</a> and we'll
          delete your submissions and confirm in writing. No forms, no
          hoops, no "retention period."
        </p>

        <h2>Questions</h2>
        <p>
          This policy is written by {BRAND.name}, for humans. If any of it
          is unclear, that's a bug — email us and we'll fix the wording.
        </p>

        <p class="muted" style="font-size: var(--text-sm);">
          Last updated: August 2026.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
